<%# THE OPENING-BALANCE CARD (onboarding step 3, main-account spec §5). One field — main's real
    balance today, entered once as the ONE ordinary entry that closes the gap between everything
    this app has tracked and the number the bank actually shows: years of income and spending
    the app never saw. Sits where `_fund_account` sits on every other account — main's own
    version of that same one-time card, and it disappears the moment the correction is written
    (`HomePresenter#awaiting_opening_balance?` is the one gate, asked here and by
    `OpeningBalancesController`).

    No form object of its own: unlike the fund-account card, every failure this door can reach
    redirects rather than re-rendering Home (see OpeningBalancesController#create), so there is
    no rejected record whose typed amount and errors need to survive a re-render — `:opening_
    balance` names the params scope on its own.

    Local: `account` (the user's own main account — the render gate has already checked it, but
    it's threaded through rather than re-read off the presenter so this partial costs no query
    of its own). %>
<%= simple_form_for :opening_balance, url: opening_balance_path do |f| %>
  <div class="px-6 py-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-3">
    <div class="flex-1">
      <%# THE HINT SAYS WHEN THE ENTRY IS DATED, and it has to, because the answer changed (Henry's
          ruling of 2026-08-20) and it is visible: the correction is one ordinary entry the user can
          find in their own history, and "recorded once, as an ordinary entry" beside a label
          reading "today" said it was dated today. It is backdated to the day before their earliest
          entry — see OpeningBalancesController#correction_date — which is also what keeps it off
          this period's Distribute screen. THE FIGURE IS STILL TODAY'S; only the entry's date is
          not, so the label above is unchanged. %>
      <%= f.input :actual,
          as: :decimal,
          label: "Main's real balance today",
          placeholder: "0.00",
          input_html: { step: 0.01 },
          hint: "What your bank shows for this account today, envelopes and all — recorded once, " \
                "as an ordinary entry dated before your earliest history so it doesn't count as " \
                "this period's income." %>
    </div>
    <div class="sm:pt-7">
      <%= f.button :submit, "Set #{account.name}'s balance", class: "btn btn-primary" %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
